<title>NETHERLANDS: VNU eyes sale of TV station interests.</title>
<headline>VNU eyes sale of TV station interests.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch publisher NV Verenigd Bezit VNU wants to sell its 44 percent interest in the loss-making Belgian television station VTM, the Dutch newspaper NRC Handelsblad reported on Saturday.</p>
<p>Quoting VNU executive Constant Busch, the newspaper also said VNU was considering selling its 38 percent interest in Dutch television stations RTL4 and RTL5.</p>
<p>&quot;We still believe in commercial television and things will improve again, but the times of high profit figures will never return,&quot; Busch was quoted as saying after a news conference to announce a move into television production.</p>
<p>VNU announced it was joining forces with Chrysalis Group Plc to set up a television production company to be called CVI Media Group.</p>
<p>Busch said his group was more interested in providing the content for television rather than broadcasting.</p>
